Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:33:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(redirect): reject empty URL userinfo

Context:
- Source review found that WHATWG URL parsing normalizes syntactically present empty userinfo to empty username and password fields.

Expected behavior:
- /u/ rejects non-empty credentials and explicit empty userinfo, including WHATWG slashless/backslash spellings.

Acceptance criteria:
- [x] https://@example.com/ returns 400.
- [x] https://:@example.com/ returns 400.
- [x] Non-canonical slashless/backslash HTTP(S) spellings return 400.
- [x] Existing accepted and rejected redirect cases remain green.

Constraints:
- Narrow review fix only; no generalized URL policy or unrelated behavior.

Validation:
- RED: focused role suite; the two empty-userinfo cases returned 302.
- GREEN: focused role suite; 20/20 passed.
- REGRESSION: complete Worker suite; 129/129 passed.
- ESLint, Prettier, TypeScript, and git diff checks passed.

Docs:
- N/A; regression cases document the edge behavior.

Refs:
- Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker#79
- Source PR #95 review finding

Upstream base:
0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6

Patch ID:
030-harden-u-redirect

Dependencies:
none
